# requirements-cuda.in: the music runtime of ACE-Step 1.5 for CUDA, linux x86_64, CPython 3.12.
# The input of scripts/release/lock-acestep.sh, which writes requirements-cuda.lock (one wheel and its sha256 per
# line). Spec: docs/specs/music.md section 3.1 and docs/specs/rebuild-kit.md section 3.2.2.
#
# Every package is pinned with ==. The list is the `pip freeze` of the spike venv (issue #505, Python 3.12.16),
# the venv that ran ACE-Step 1.5 on ai-n2. Do not add a range: the kit installs offline with --require-hashes.
# The +cu128 packages come from the PyTorch CUDA 12.8 index; everything else from PyPI.
#
# Not here, on purpose:
#   - ace-step 1.5.0 and nano-vllm 0.2.0 have no wheel on any index: ark sync builds them from the pinned commit of
#     ACE-Step/ACE-Step-1.5 (the `builds` of the kit item in catalog/ark.yaml) and adds them to the lock it writes
#     into the kit, with the sha256 of the wheels it built.
#   - the shim (engines/acestep, localai-music-shim) is built by ark sync from this repository at the catalog tag.
#
# The build backends at the end are not part of the spike venv: ark sync needs them, offline, to build the three
# wheels above with `pip wheel --no-build-isolation` (hatchling for ace-step, setuptools for nano-vllm and the
# shim; setuptools is also an ACE-Step dependency; hatchling also needs packaging and tomlkit, pinned above).
